kindspec/.github is licensed per directory. This is deliberate, not an oversight.

  AGENTS.md, STATE.md,
  README.md, profile/       CC-BY-4.0
  scripts/                  MIT

profile/ includes the org mark in profile/assets/. Anything else in this
repository that is a document rather than code is CC-BY-4.0.

Full texts are in LICENSES/. Source files carry SPDX headers.

WHY THE SPLIT

It follows the split every kindspec repository uses: prose under CC-BY-4.0, so
the contract can be copied and adapted with attribution; code under MIT. The
contract is meant to be reused — a rule other projects can lift is worth more
than one they have to rewrite.
